    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths holds a dual role for me—both as a practical tool from my childhood studies (though I stopped formally in school) and a philosophical puzzle. It’s the kind of subject that feels concrete yet open-ended, like solving equations is part problem-solving but also about unlocking patterns in reality. I’m not naturally anxious about it; instead, it intrigues me because its abstract nature mirrors how I enjoy connecting ideas through logic.",
